1
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:18,000
An epic story of three brothers. Bound by blood.
Divided by fate. Driven by destiny.

2
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Bound by Honor is a crime, action, drama film directed by Taylor Hackford.

3
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Based on the true life experiences of poet Jimmy Santiago Baca, the film focuses
on half-brothers Paco and Cruz, and their bi-racial cousin Miklo.

4
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:54,000
It opens in 1972, as the three are members of an East L.A.

5
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
gang known as the "Vatos Locos", and the story focuses on how a violent
crime and the influence of narcotics alter their lives.

6
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Miklo is incarcerated and sent to San Quentin,
where he makes a "home" for himself.

7
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
Cruz becomes an exceptional artist, but a heroin
addiction overcomes him with tragic results.

8
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:42,000
Paco becomes a cop and an enemy to his "carnal", Miklo.

9
01:04:48,000 --> 01:04:54,000
Miklo, played by Damian Chapa.

10
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Cruz, played by Jesse Borrego.

11
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
Paco, played by Benjamin Bratt.

12
01:26:24,000 --> 01:26:30,000
Montana, played by Enrique Castillo.

13
01:33:36,000 --> 01:33:42,000
Magic Mike, played by Victor Rivers.

14
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
Bonafide, played by Delroy Lindo.

15
01:48:00,000 --> 01:48:06,000
Blood In Blood Out (also known as Bound by Honor and Blood In Blood Out: Bound By Honor) is a 1993 American epic crime
drama film directed by Taylor Hackford, from a screenplay co-written by Jimmy Santiago Baca  and Floyd Mutrux.

16
01:55:12,000 --> 01:55:18,000
The film follows the intertwining lives of three
Chicano relatives from 1972 to 1984.

17
02:02:24,000 --> 02:02:30,000
They start out as members of a street gang in East Los Angeles, and as dramatic
incidents occur, their lives and friendships are forever changed.

18
02:09:36,000 --> 02:09:42,000
The film stars Jesse Borrego, Benjamin Bratt,
Enrique Castillo, and Damian Chapa.

19
02:16:48,000 --> 02:16:54,000
The screenplay is partly autobiographical, drawn from Baca’s
experiences in street gangs and imprisonment.

20
02:24:00,000 --> 02:24:06,000
The film's title refers to the initiation ritual of having to kill someone to enter a gang
and, on the reverse end, not being able to leave the gang unless killed.

21
02:31:12,000 --> 02:31:18,000
The film was released by Buena Vista Pictures Distribution on April 30, 1993.

22
02:38:24,000 --> 02:38:30,000
Critical reviews were mixed to positive, and Blood In Blood Out was a box office disappointment,
but later became a cult classic film  among parts of the Mexican-American community.

23
02:45:36,000 --> 02:45:42,000
The film explores themes of street gang, ghetto, juvenile prison, artist, jail.

24
02:52:48,000 --> 02:52:54,000
The tone is intense and dark and emotional.
